  "worked_solution": "To calculate the $x$-intercepts, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ We do this and solve the resulting equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+12x+4y & =28 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(0)^{2}+12x+4(0) & =28 \\\\ {x}^{2}+12x & =28 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+12x+36)-36 & =28 \\\\ (x+6)^{2}-36 & =28 \\\\ (x+6)^{2} & =64 \\\\ x+6 & =\\pm 8 \\\\ x & =-6\\pm 8 \\\\ x & =-14,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the $x$-intercepts are\n\n$$\nA(-14,0)\\,\\text{and}\\,B(2,0).\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
